{"chunk_id": "d8efca9d3dac", "text": "On the seventh day of the curse upon King Parikshit, the sage Kasyapa travels to save the king from the serpent Takshaka\u2019s deadly bite. Takshaka intercepts him and demonstrates the power of his venom by burning a banyan tree to ashes; Kasyapa proves his own power by restoring it. Fearing humiliation if the king were revived, Takshaka bribes Kasyapa with greater wealth to turn back. Disguised, the serpent then kills Parikshit despite all precautions. When Janamejaya later hears how his father might have been saved, grief turns into fury. Convinced that Takshaka maliciously prevented the rescue, the king resolves on revenge and announces a massive snake-sacrifice meant to destroy Takshaka and the entire serpent race.\nTakshaka bribes sage Kasyapa to abandon curing King Parikshit, kills the king, and Janamejaya resolves to avenge him with a snake\u2011sacrifice.\nThemes: revenge, corruption and bribery, fate vs intervention, royal grief, vengeance ritual", "vector": [0.01904039829969406, -0.005952673032879829, -0.0010804509511217475, 0.0006858994602225721, -0.01837446168065071, 0.00321926805190742, -0.013617758639156818, -0.01365173514932394, -0.008045622147619724, -0.016431007534265518, 0.015384533442556858, 0.0040194131433963776, 0.020562544465065002, 0.0165125522762537, 0.008331024087965488, -0.0039208815433084965, 0.05131801962852478, -0.005765802692621946, 0.024857165291905403, -0.0005508430767804384, -0.009703672491014004, 0.002293410012498498, 0.0052901324816048145, 0.023321431130170822, -0.010403587482869625, 0.024952299892902374, 7.076656038407236e-05, -0.02003251202404499, 0.018347280099987984, -0.00947263278067112, -0.014134200289845467, -0.01860550045967102, -0.012476149946451187, -0.012292677536606789, -0.03655865415930748, 0.003416331484913826, -0.013943932950496674, -0.0023834474850445986, 0.013617758639156818, -0.00975123979151249, 0.0019366572378203273, -0.0016079351771622896, -0.011545195244252682, 0.01264603